#
# Five subjects s1..s5 carrying {30, 10, 50, 20, 40} — a permutation DELIBERATELY
# uncorrelated with subject order in either direction, so neither ascending nor
# descending `ORDER BY ?s` can coincide with the minimum/maximum by construction.
# `agg-stat-first-last.rq`'s inner subquery orders `DESC(?s)` (mirroring
# `:groupConcatOrder`'s own `ORDER BY DESC(?s)`, for the same reason: a regression
# that silently fell back to load/scan order — ascending `s1..s5`, i.e. the file
# order below — would read a DIFFERENT, wrong FIRST/LAST rather than coincidentally
# passing). Under `DESC(?s)` the row sequence is s5,s4,s3,s2,s1, i.e. values
# 40, 20, 50, 10, 30 — so FIRST = 40 and LAST = 30, each distinct from the group's
# MIN (10), MAX (50), each other, and the file/ascending-scan order's own first (30)
# and last (40) values.
@prefix : <https://example.org/agg-stat#> .

:s1 :value 30 .
:s2 :value 10 .
:s3 :value 50 .
:s4 :value 20 .
:s5 :value 40 .
